## Bug Analysis & Fix Summary

### Root Cause

In `ExperienceTweaks.java`, the gesture detector's tap handlers (`onSingleTapUp` and `onSingleTapConfirmed`) gated the `doAction("display-history")` call behind the `history-onclick` preference:

```java
// BEFORE (buggy): history-onclick gates the entire method call
if (prefs.getBoolean("history-onclick", false)) {
    doAction("display-history");
}
```

The `doAction("display-history")` method has two responsibilities:
1. Run `HistorySearcher` (gated by `history-onclick` — correct)
2. Show the favorites bar when minimalistic mode for favorites is enabled (NOT gated — **correct behavior**)

Since `history-onclick` was the only gate for the entire method, the favorites bar never appeared on tap when `history-onclick` was disabled — even though showing the favorites bar should work independently.

### Fix

Moved the `history-onclick` check from the tap handlers **into** the `doAction("display-history")` case, wrapping only the `HistorySearcher` block. This way:
- The favorites bar shows on tap whenever `isMinimalisticModeEnabledForFavorites()` is true, regardless of `history-onclick`
- The `HistorySearcher` still only runs when `history-onclick` is explicitly enabled

### Final Patch

```diff
--- a/app/src/main/java/fr/neamar/kiss/forwarder/ExperienceTweaks.java
+++ app/src/main/java/fr/neamar/kiss/forwarder/ExperienceTweaks.java
@@ -75,9 +75,7 @@
             public boolean onSingleTapUp(MotionEvent e) {
                 // Double tap disabled: display history directly
                 if(!prefs.getBoolean("double-tap", false)) {
-                    if (prefs.getBoolean("history-onclick", false)) {
-                        doAction("display-history");
-                    }
+                    doAction("display-history");
                 }
                 return super.onSingleTapUp(e);
             }
@@ -86,9 +84,7 @@
             public boolean onSingleTapConfirmed(MotionEvent e) {
                 // Double tap enabled: wait to confirm this is indeed a single tap, not a double tap
                 if(prefs.getBoolean("double-tap", false)) {
-                    if (prefs.getBoolean("history-onclick", false)) {
-                        doAction("display-history");
-                    }
+                    doAction("display-history");
                 }

                 return super.onSingleTapConfirmed(e);
@@ -155,15 +151,17 @@
                         }
                         break;
                     case "display-history":
-                        // if minimalistic mode is enabled,
-                        if (isMinimalisticModeEnabled()) {
-                            // and we're currently in minimalistic mode with no results,
-                            // and we're not looking at the app list
-                            if (mainActivity.isViewingSearchResults() && mainActivity.searchEditText.getText().toString().isEmpty()) {
-                                if (mainActivity.list.getAdapter() == null || mainActivity.list.getAdapter().isEmpty()) {
-                                    mainActivity.runTask(new HistorySearcher(mainActivity));
-                                    mainActivity.clearButton.setVisibility(View.VISIBLE);
-                                    mainActivity.menuButton.setVisibility(View.INVISIBLE);
+                        // Run history search only if history-onclick is enabled
+                        if (prefs.getBoolean("history-onclick", false)) {
+                            if (isMinimalisticModeEnabled()) {
+                                // and we're currently in minimalistic mode with no results,
+                                // and we're not looking at the app list
+                                if (mainActivity.isViewingSearchResults() && mainActivity.searchEditText.getText().toString().isEmpty()) {
+                                    if (mainActivity.list.getAdapter() == null || mainActivity.list.getAdapter().isEmpty()) {
+                                        mainActivity.runTask(new HistorySearcher(mainActivity));
+                                        mainActivity.clearButton.setVisibility(View.VISIBLE);
+                                        mainActivity.menuButton.setVisibility(View.INVISIBLE);
+                                    }
                                 }
                             }
                         }
```

### Build Note

The project requires network access to resolve the Android Gradle Plugin 3.6.2 from `jcenter()` (now deprecated/unreachable). All network connections are blocked in this environment. When the patch is applied to a build-capable environment, the project should compile without code errors since only logic was moved around — no new types, methods, or imports were added.

